            <ArticleTitle>Unexpected lumbar abscess due to scarification wet cupping: a case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>645-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.ctim.2014.07.001</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0965-2299(14)00109-5</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="OBJECTIVE" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">This case presents a rare cause of lumbar abscess.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="METHODS" NlmCategory="METHODS">A 51-year-old male patient was admitted to the emergency department with a complaint of lumbar pain. Spinal magnetic resonance imaging revealed a lumbar abscess.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">The abscess was treated with drainage of the abscess and antibiotic.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSION" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">Scarification wet cupping therapy should be taken into consideration as a rare cause of lumbar abscesses in patients who present with skin findings indicative of scarification. Scarification wet cupping therapy practitioners must pay attention to hygienic measures.</AbstractText>
